        "referee": "John Brooks",
        "standfirst": "Coventry City beat Newcastle United 4-1 for their first home win, climbing out of relegation places.",
        "account": "Jack Rudoni put Coventry City ahead from the spot after six minutes, sending his kick low into the corner with his left. Just after half-time Sidiki Cherif doubled the lead, beating the goalkeeper with a low right-foot strike from outside the box.\nSven Botman pulled one back for Newcastle United 20 minutes from time, meeting a pass from Nico González with a shot from distance that flew into the top corner. Ellis Simms, a substitute for Cherif, answered after 81 minutes, turning in Brandon Thomas-Asante's pass from close range. Stephen Mfuni, on for Matt Grimes, made it 4-1 after 86 minutes, turning in a ball from Jay Dasilva inside the box for a second Coventry goal in five minutes. Bazoumana Touré went off injured for Newcastle one minute into stoppage time.",
